  "prefLabel": "Bcr 207.05 Right to Counsel",
  "priorExpiration": "2012-07-16",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Bcr 207.05 Right to Counsel.\n\n(a) Parties and witnesses in an adjudicative proceeding may be represented by counsel, but an attorney appearing on behalf of a party shall first file a letter announcing the fact of representation at the earliest date practical.\n\n(b) Requests for appointment of counsel shall not be entertained, and the board shall have no responsibility for the legal expenses of any licensee, applicant, intervenor or witness.\n\nSource. #8044, eff 2-17-04; ss by #10073, INTERIM, eff 1-17-12, EXPIRES: 7-16-12; ss by #10161, eff 7-13-12",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/bcr200.html"
